# T0047 — Project Overview changes

**Task:** T0047 (`id` 47) — Project Overview changes  
**State at plan:** `ready` · priority `medium` · projectId 4  
**Branch (on approval):** `T0047-project-overview`

## Problem

Project Overview has three UX issues:

1. Status values display in lowercase (`idea`, `active`, …).
2. The Edit pencil sits above the title instead of inline on the title row; Overview also duplicates the page-head `h1`.
3. An “Enabled views” jump card on Overview duplicates module navigation that belongs only under Settings.

## Goal

Polish Overview: capitalized status labels, title-row Edit control, and Settings-only module management (no Overview jump card).

## Scope

**In**

- `client/src/pages/ProjectDetailPage.tsx` (Overview tab primarily):
  - Capitalize Status **display** labels in the edit `<select>` and in view-mode status text (`Idea`, `Active`, `Paused`, `Done`). Keep API/DB values lowercase; retain `idea` as a valid option.
  - Place pencil (and Cancel / Save overview in edit mode) on the same row as the in-card project title, far right.
  - On Overview, omit the redundant `page-head` title (card title + inline actions become the primary header).
  - Remove the Overview “Enabled views” card entirely.

**Out**

- Removing or migrating status `idea`
- Schema / API status enum changes
- Settings tab module hub changes
- Adding a “Status:” label in view mode
- Other project tabs’ page-head titles (Images, Settings, modules keep current page-head unless they already rely on shared markup — only Overview hides the duplicate)

## Decisions (user)

1. ~~Remove Status `idea`~~ — **dropped**; task description + comment updated on PROD.
2. Capitalize display labels only; lowercase API values unchanged.
3. Pencil on in-card title row (far right); drop redundant page-head title on Overview.
4. Remove Overview “Enabled views” card; Settings tab unchanged.
5. No “Status:” label in view mode.

## Approach

1. Add a small label map (or `capitalize` helper) for the four status values; use it in the select option text and read-only status line.
2. Restructure Overview card header: one row with `h1.wiki-page-title` + actions (`wiki-panel__main-actions`); remove the empty head that currently only holds actions. In edit mode, keep name field in the form; title row can still show current saved name + Cancel/Save, or show actions beside a static title — prefer actions on the title row in both modes for consistency.
3. Conditionally render `page-head` only when `tab !== "overview"` (or leave an empty/minimal head) so Overview is not double-titled.
4. Delete the “Enabled views” card block and any now-unused bits tied only to that UI.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Status select shows Idea / Active / Paused / Done; values still `idea` / `active` / `paused` / `done`.
- [ ] View mode shows capitalized status (no Status label).
- [ ] Pencil is inline far-right of the project title on Overview; Cancel/Save sit there in edit mode.
- [ ] Overview has a single title (no duplicate page-head + card title).
- [ ] Overview has no “Enabled views” section; Settings still enables/disables modules and middle nav still works.

## QA checklist (post-implement)

1. Open a project Overview: one title row with pencil on the right.
2. Edit → Cancel/Save on that row; save status/name/description still works.
3. Status options and view text are capitalized; saving still stores lowercase.
4. Confirm no “Enabled views” card on Overview; open Settings and toggle a module — middle nav updates as before.
5. Spot-check another tab (e.g. Tasks/Settings) still shows a normal page-head title.
